{
    "chapter_num": 5,
    "verses_count": 20,
    "paragraphs_list": [
        {
            "type": "section_header",
            "text": "Reverence, Humility, and Contentment"
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 1,
                    "num_str": "1",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Ch 4.17 in Heb"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " Guard your steps when you go to the house of God; to draw near to listen is better than to offer the sacrifice of fools; for they do not know that they are doing evil. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 2,
                    "num_str": "2",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Ch 5.1 in Heb"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Be not rash with your mouth, nor let your heart be hasty to utter a word before God, for God is in heaven, and you upon earth; therefore let your words be few."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 3,
                    "num_str": "3",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For a dream comes with much business, and a fool’s voice with many words."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 4,
                    "num_str": "4",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When you vow a vow to God, do not delay paying it; for he has no pleasure in fools. Pay what you vow. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 5,
                    "num_str": "5",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "It is better that you should not vow than that you should vow and not pay. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 6,
                    "num_str": "6",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Let not your mouth lead you into sin, and do not say before the messenger"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or angel"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " that it was a mistake; why should God be angry at your voice, and destroy the work of your hands?"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 7,
                    "num_str": "7",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For when dreams increase, empty words grow many:"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or For in a multitude of dreams there is futility, and ruin in a flood of words"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " but do you fear God."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 8,
                    "num_str": "8",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "If you see in a province the poor oppressed and justice and right violently taken away, do not be amazed at the matter; for the high official is watched by a higher, and there are yet higher ones over them. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 9,
                    "num_str": "9",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "But in all, a king is an advantage to a land with cultivated fields."
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Or The profit of the land is among all of them; a cultivated field has a king"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 10,
                    "num_str": "10",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "He who loves money will not be satisfied with money; nor he who loves wealth, with gain: this also is vanity."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 11,
                    "num_str": "11",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "When goods increase, they increase who eat them; and what gain has their owner but to see them with his eyes?"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 12,
                    "num_str": "12",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Sweet is the sleep of a laborer, whether he eats little or much; but the surfeit of the rich will not let him sleep."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 13,
                    "num_str": "13",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "There is a grievous evil which I have seen under the sun: riches were kept by their owner to his hurt, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 14,
                    "num_str": "14",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and those riches were lost in a bad venture; and he is father of a son, but he has nothing in his hand. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 15,
                    "num_str": "15",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "As he came from his mother’s womb he shall go again, naked as he came, and shall take nothing for his toil, which he may carry away in his hand. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 16,
                    "num_str": "16",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "This also is a grievous evil: just as he came, so shall he go; and what gain has he that he toiled for the wind, "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 17,
                    "num_str": "17",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "and spent all his days in darkness and grief,"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "FOOTNOTE",
                            "text": "Gk: Heb all his days also he eats in darkness"
                        },
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": " in much vexation and sickness and resentment?"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        },
        {
            "type": "section_paragraph",
            "verses_list": [
                {
                    "num_int": 18,
                    "num_str": "18",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Behold, what I have seen to be good and to be fitting is to eat and drink and find enjoyment in all the toil with which one toils under the sun the few days of his life which God has given him, for this is his lot. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 19,
                    "num_str": "19",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "Every man also to whom God has given wealth and possessions and power to enjoy them, and to accept his lot and find enjoyment in his toil—this is the gift of God. "
                        }
                    ]
                },
                {
                    "num_int": 20,
                    "num_str": "20",
                    "verse_parts": [
                        {
                            "style": "NONE",
                            "text": "For he will not much remember the days of his life because God keeps him occupied with joy in his heart."
                        }
                    ]
                }
            ]
        }
    ]
}